---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FloodlitShell from '../components/FloodlitShell.astro';

const title = 'Privacy: what Beat My 11 stores | Beat My 11';
const description =
  'What Beat My 11 stores: your draft stays in your browser; we keep anonymous scores and page counts, and a leaderboard name only if you choose to add one.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <FloodlitShell>
    <article class="pv">
      <p class="fs-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="fs-title">Your XI, <span class="fs-hl">your business.</span></h1>
      <p class="fs-lede">Beat My 11 has no accounts and no ads. Here is everything it stores.</p>

      <h2>On your device</h2>
      <p>
        Your draft in progress and your finished XI are saved in your browser’s local storage so you can
        close the tab and come back. They never leave your device unless you share them. “Draft again”
        clears them.
      </p>

      <h2>Anonymous scores</h2>
      <p>
        When a Test series from the spin draft is played, we record one anonymous row: a short fingerprint of the XI (so the same
        XI isn’t counted twice), the two team scores, the series scoreline and the time. We use these
        only to tune how hard the game is. The row has no name, account, IP address or cookie attached
        to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Page counts</h2>
      <p>
        We keep daily totals, for each game (Test, ODI, T20I, IPL and Pick any XI), of how many times the
        home, draft, result, pick and shared-link pages were opened, how often the share button was
        tapped, and how many daily challenges and friend challenges were started and finished. These
        are plain counters, not tied to a person.
      </p>

      <h2>Daily leaderboard</h2>
      <p>
        After a Daily Challenge you can choose to add your result to that day’s leaderboard. Nothing is
        sent unless you press the button. If you do, we store your overall score, the series scoreline, a
        short fingerprint of your XI, the name you typed and the time. The name is optional and
        <strong>is shown publicly</strong> on the leaderboard; leave it blank to appear as “Anonymous”.
        Your browser also keeps a random code (not linked to you) so the same browser cannot enter the
        same day twice. We do not store your IP address with the entry. To have an entry or a name
        removed, email <a href="mailto:hello@beatmy11.com">hello@beatmy11.com</a> with the day and the
        name you used. Scores are worked out on your device and cannot be checked, so the leaderboard is
        for fun. If your browser sends “Do Not Track”, the button is not offered.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        A share link contains the players in your XI in its address, so whoever opens the link can see
        that XI. Nothing else about you is in it.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site runs on Cloudflare, which, like any web host, processes ordinary request data such as IP
        addresses to deliver pages and protect the site. We don’t use it to identify anyone. If your
        browser sends “Do Not Track”, the site doesn’t send the anonymous scores or counts at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Data sources</h2>
      <p>
        ODI, T20I and IPL match data: <a href="https://cricsheet.org">Cricsheet</a> (cricsheet.org), used under the
        Open Data Commons Attribution licence. Totals leave out matches Cricsheet withholds.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@beatmy11.com">hello@beatmy11.com</a>.</p>
      <p class="pv-updated">Last updated 2 October 2026.</p>
    </article>
  </FloodlitShell>

  <style is:global>
    .pv { margin: 6vh auto 0; text-align: left; }
    .pv .fs-eyebrow, .pv .fs-title, .pv .fs-lede { text-align: center; }
    .pv h2 { margin: 28px 0 6px; font: 600 15px Inter, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--fs-text); }
    .pv p { margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--fs-muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
    .pv a { color: var(--fs-lime); }
    .pv .pv-updated { margin-top: 28px; color: var(--fs-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
